# 02 -- Church numerals and arithmetic
# A numeral n is the function that applies its first argument n times:
#   0 = λf.λx.x      1 = λf.λx.f x      2 = λf.λx.f (f x) ...
# Try:  python lambda_calculus.py examples/02_numerals.lc

run ZERO
run SUCC TWO
run ADD TWO THREE
run MULT TWO THREE
run POWER TWO THREE

# Subtraction is the tricky one: PRED rebuilds n-1 from scratch using a pair
# that carries (current, previous) -- Kleene's trick.
run PRED THREE
run SUB FIVE TWO
run SUB TWO FIVE
